WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.299
J.R.R.

00:00:01.299 --> 00:00:02.299
Tolkien: Father of Modern Fantasy
By: Crystal Sullivan

00:00:02.299 --> 00:00:04.550
Known as ‘the father of modern fantasy’
his epic tales of legend and lore have been

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:09.540
enjoyed by millions of people all over the
world — devoured in popular books and adapted

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.700
for Hollywood blockbuster films.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.539
Unbelievably bright, he was a distinguished
university professor, poet, historian, and

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:17.880
expert linguist.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.619
As a child, he even made up his own languages
for pure fun.

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:27.069
He gave us complex and fanciful creatures
including hobbits, orcs, and elves set in

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:29.119
an prehistoric Middle-earth.

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:34.300
Some theorize his made up worlds are symbolic
of his country’s past power struggles, influenced

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.929
by his devout Roman Catholic faith, or simply
the genesis of his personal experiences.

00:00:39.929 --> 00:00:45.489
In any case, there is no denying his glorious
imagination and his rightful place among the

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:47.570
greatest writers of all time.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.739
But who was the creator of The Hobbit and
the Lord of the Rings?

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:57.609
Today on Biographics we explore the life of
J.R.R.

00:00:57.609 --> 00:00:59.999
Tolkien.

00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:07.120
Formative Years
Before bank clerk Arthur Tolkien and Mabel

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.820
Suffield welcomed their son into the world,
the English couple moved to South Africa.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.920
Here, Arthur had high hopes of advancing his
career and providing a comfortable life for

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.240
their budding family.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.930
John Ronald Reuel (known as “Ronald” to
most) was born in Bloemfontein, South Africa

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.390
on January 3, 1892.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:27.900
Not long after, another son Hilary was born,
completing the Tolkien family.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.020
Tolkien’s childhood in Africa was cut short
when his mother decided the boys would be

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.140
better educated in their native England.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.220
At the age of three, Tolkien and his mother
and younger brother left for their homeland

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.130
while Arthur stayed behind to settle the business.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:45.790
He was planning to join them but never made
it -- falling ill and dying of a severe brain

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:50.390
hemorrhage (a complication of rheumatic fever)
on February 15, 1896.

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:55.240
At the time, the spread of disease and contagions
were feared and travel took many weeks, if

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.240
not months.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.530
Arthur’s body was laid to rest without family
by his side.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:03.950
Having spent just a small fraction of his
early years in Africa, Tolkien had few memories

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:05.140
from the time.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:09.000
However, one tale persists yet the facts remain
uncertain.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.250
According to the story, the then-toddler Tolkien
stumbled upon and was bit by a baboon spider

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.670
(a kind of tarantula) in the garden.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:21.530
Tolkien ran screaming and his nurse immediately
snatched him up and sucked the venom out from

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:22.530
the wound.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.830
Tolkien later said, “...he could remember
a hot day and running in fear through long,

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:31.390
dead grass, but the memory of the tarantula
itself faded, and he said that the incident

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.280
left him with no especial dislike of spiders.”

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:39.560
Still, fans and armchair psychologists alike
speculate whether the tarantula influenced

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.130
the presence of man-eating spiders in Tolkien’s
later fictional works.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:48.080
Back in England, Mabel and the boys settled
with family in the West Midlands — first

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.260
in Kings Heath and then in Sarehole.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:54.670
On one hand, and especially in the city of
Birmingham, the West Midlands was urban, dark,

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:55.690
and industrial.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.230
On the other hand, it was the idyllic English
countryside with

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:03.450
lush with green grass, trees, and a corn mill
in the rural hamlet of Sarehole.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:07.860
Between the ages of four and eight, Tolkien
lived across the street and within 300 yards

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.520
of the Sarehole Mill and Moseley Bog.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:14.200
He spent many hours playing there with his
younger brother — and being chased by the

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.840
miller’s son, whom the boys nicknamed the
“White Ogre.”

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.600
The Shire, Tolkien’s imaginary land of Hobbits,
was inspired by Sarehole.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.600
In The Hobbit, he writes of Bilbo Baggins
"running as fast as his furry feet could carry

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:31.370
him down the lane, past the great Mill, across
The Water and then on for a mile or more."

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.930
Tolkien’s mother homeschooled the boys at
first, teaching the young Tolkien botany and

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.180
the basics of Latin.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:40.069
Tolkien could read fluently by the age of
four and write soon after.

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:44.890
He loved drawing landscapes and trees but
his favorite studies were those involving

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:45.890
languages.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:49.810
Later, he would attend King Edward’s School
in Birmingham which proved to be the perfect

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:54.310
breeding ground for the boy’s natural curiosity
and development of linguistics.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:58.750
Tolkien was an exceptional student who was
capable of easily mastering ancient and modern

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:03.730
languages including Greek, Latin, Spanish,
Old English, Old Norse, Gothic and Finnish.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:08.020
The boy made up his own languages, including
early variations of Elvish ones featured in

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.020
his writings.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:13.490
At King Edwards, he made a number of close
friends and formed a semi-secret society that

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:17.209
enjoyed drinking tea and critiquing each other’s
literary works.

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:23.710
They called themselves T.C.B.S. (which stood
for the Tea Club and Barrovian Society).

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:27.860
Despite the earlier loss of his father, life
for the young Tolkien was generally happy

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:30.669
until two events altered the course of his
life.

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:34.220
In 1900, his mother decided to convert to
the Catholic faith.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:39.789
This bold move left Mabel and her sons estranged
from both sides of the family and in the fallout,

00:04:39.789 --> 00:04:43.610
Tolkien experienced isolation, loneliness,
and poverty.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:47.840
Following his acceptance into the Catholic
church, Tolkien remained devout in his faith

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.249
for the rest of his life.

00:04:49.249 --> 00:04:53.090
And, he has been credited with being partly
responsible for bringing another famous writer

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.469
and friend, C.S.

00:04:54.469 --> 00:04:56.210
Lewis, back to Christianity.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:05:01.020
Tragedy struck Tolkien again in 1904 when
his mother was diagnosed with diabetes — a

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.569
sure death sentence for most before insulin
was available.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.460
Sadly, Mabel died in the same year, on November
14.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:08.520
Tolkien was 12 at the time.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:13.259
Fortunately for Tolkien and his brother Hilary,
their Catholic priest Father Francis Morgan

00:05:13.259 --> 00:05:17.659
stepped in and became their guardian and made
sure the boys received everything they needed

00:05:17.659 --> 00:05:20.559
— both materially and spiritually.

00:05:20.559 --> 00:05:24.210
Lúthien and Beren

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:28.169
Tolkien met his eventual bride Edith Bratt
when he was 16, and she was 19.

00:05:28.169 --> 00:05:33.240
They were both orphans and lodgers at a boarding
house run by a woman named Mrs. Faulkner.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:36.370
The two grew fond of each other and a friendship
developed.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:40.039
And then, as it happens with teenagers, the
pair became too close for Father Francis’

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:41.039
liking.

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:45.539
He was horrified his ward was courting a Protestant
woman and believed the relationship was a

00:05:45.539 --> 00:05:47.960
distraction from Tolkien’s school work.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:52.789
Father Francis forbade Tolkien to see or correspond
with Edith until he was 21.

00:05:52.789 --> 00:05:56.139
This was a devastating blow to Tolkien but
he obeyed the order.

00:05:56.139 --> 00:05:59.860
When his birthday approached, he wrote to
his love and proposed marriage.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:04.240
Her reply was heartbreaking but offered a
glimmer of hope, she was engaged to another

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.080
man but his letter made her reconsider.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:12.229
Edith agreed to meet Tolkien on January 8,
1913 at the train station in Cheltenham.

00:06:12.229 --> 00:06:16.249
They walked and talked for hours and Edith
accepted Tolkien’s marriage proposal — breaking

00:06:16.249 --> 00:06:17.819
off her prior engagement.

00:06:17.819 --> 00:06:23.259
Edith converted to Catholicism and the couple
married on March 22, 1916.

00:06:23.259 --> 00:06:27.020
Tolkien was 24 years old, and a few months
shy of deploying to the Western Front.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:31.819
In a letter to his son Michael years later,
“Tolkien expressed admiration for his wife's

00:06:31.819 --> 00:06:36.919
willingness to marry a man with no job, little
money, and no prospects except the likelihood

00:06:36.919 --> 00:06:39.259
of being killed in the Great War.”

00:06:39.259 --> 00:06:42.560
Tolkien was a true romantic and Edith was
his muse.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:46.740
He wrote of her, “...her hair was raven,
her skin clear, her eyes brighter than you

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:50.039
have seen them, and she could sing — and
dance.”

00:06:50.039 --> 00:06:54.419
Tolkien was so mad for Edith he created the
fictional pair of star-crossed lovers based

00:06:54.419 --> 00:06:59.339
on their romance: Lúthien, daughter of the
Elven King of Doriath, and Beren, a mortal

00:06:59.339 --> 00:07:00.339
man.

00:07:00.339 --> 00:07:04.339
They fall for each other when Beren discovers
Lúthien singing and dancing in a glade.

00:07:04.339 --> 00:07:07.830
Yet, their love can never be since Beren is
destined to die.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:12.639
Alas, her disapproving father the King sends
Beren on a task he knows the man cannot complete.

00:07:12.639 --> 00:07:16.689
The full story of Lúthien and Beren was left
unfinished during Tolkien’s lifetime but

00:07:16.689 --> 00:07:19.059
served as an important backstory in The Hobbit.

00:07:19.059 --> 00:07:23.139
Tolkien’s son Christopher later published
Lúthien and Beren as a chapter of the saga,

00:07:23.139 --> 00:07:24.270
The Silmarillion.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:28.319
Edith and Tolkien enjoyed a long and happy
marriage to each other and they had four children:

00:07:28.319 --> 00:07:32.479
John Francis, Michael Hilary, Christopher
John, and Priscilla Mary Anne.

00:07:32.479 --> 00:07:36.740
Tolkien was a devoted father and loved his
children, often making up fanciful stories

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:37.740
for them.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:44.350
From 1920 to 1942 at Christmas time, Tolkien
illustrated letters to his children...introducing

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.270
new characters such as the North Polar Bear,
Snow Man and others, each year.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:51.050
Three years after his death, these intimate
stories were published as Letters from Father

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.639
Christmas by the Tolkien estate.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:59.319
The Great War
Believing he was in his own words, "a young

00:07:59.319 --> 00:08:04.569
man with too much imagination and little physical
courage," Tolkien did not rush to join the

00:08:04.569 --> 00:08:06.639
British military when war broke out.

00:08:06.639 --> 00:08:11.620
Instead, he returned to Oxford where he had
achieved a first-class degree in June of 1915.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:16.020
Tolkien was busy working on poems and his
invented languages at the time.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:20.310
Eventually though, Tolkien enlisted as a second
lieutenant in the Lancashire Fusiliers and

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:25.009
was sent to active duty on the Western Front
just in time for the Battle of the Somme (also

00:08:25.009 --> 00:08:26.649
known as the Somme Offensive).

00:08:26.649 --> 00:08:31.249
The Battle of the Somme remains one of the
bloodiest military battles in history.

00:08:31.249 --> 00:08:37.050
It lasted four long months and on the first
day alone, British troops suffered over 57,000

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:38.050
casualties.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:44.600
In total, over a million men lost their lives
including 420,000 British soldiers.

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.250
Fighting in the Great War, Tolkien witnesses
the horrors of trench fighting and lived in

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.509
deplorable, unsanitary conditions.

00:08:50.509 --> 00:08:54.740
It was hell on earth for Tolkien and his comrades
who stood by as their friends suffered and

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:56.250
died alongside them.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:00.980
They spent their days and nights with little
relief and endured infestations of lice that

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:02.470
feasted on their flesh.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:06.720
As a result, Tolkien came down with “trench
fever,” a major medical problem of World

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:07.720
War I.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:11.100
So severe was the lice, a chaplain staying
with Tolkien’s unit later recalled:

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:14.060
“... We dossed down for the night in the
hopes of getting some sleep, but it was not

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:15.060
to be.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:17.840
We no sooner lay down than hordes of lice
got up.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:22.000
So we went round to the Medical Officer, who
was also in the dugout with his equipment,

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:26.329
and he gave us some ointment which he assured
us would keep the little brutes away.

00:09:26.329 --> 00:09:30.990
We anointed ourselves all over with the stuff
and again lay down in great hopes, but it

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:35.680
was not to be, because instead of discouraging
them it seemed to act like a kind of hors

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:40.140
d'oeuvre and the little beggars went at their
feast with renewed vigour.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:43.949
Sick and unable to fight, Tolkien left the
battlefront to recover in a Birmingham hospital

00:09:43.949 --> 00:09:45.509
in November of 1916.

00:09:45.509 --> 00:09:50.400
Through 1917 and 1918 Tolkien had recurring
bouts of the illness and he spent the time

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.680
in remission doing service at home and at
various camps.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:58.140
Tolkien most likely escaped death on the battlefront
precisely because he became ill.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:03.570
Sadly, all but one of his close friends, including
those from the T.C.B.S., perished in the war.

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:08.829
As a writer, this tragedy of loss and first-hand
experience in battle provided Tolkien with

00:10:08.829 --> 00:10:10.649
a keen sense of awareness.

00:10:10.649 --> 00:10:14.790
From the unpublished, The Book of Lost Tales,
Tolkien writes, “… in huts full of blasphemy

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:20.459
and smut, or by candle light in bell-tents,
even some down in dugouts under shell fire.”

00:10:20.459 --> 00:10:25.029
In The Hobbit, The Battle of the Five Armies
is thought to draw upon Tolkien’s wartime

00:10:25.029 --> 00:10:29.889
experiences, as well as the Dead Marshes and
Black Gate of Mordor in The Lord of the Rings.

00:10:29.889 --> 00:10:34.730
On November 11, 1918, the Armistice was signed
marking the end of World War I.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:39.550
The Professor

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:43.980
Tolkien was appointed Assistant Lexicographer
on the New English Dictionary (the “Oxford

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:47.800
English Dictionary”) in 1918 but stayed
on the job for only a short while.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:52.400
In the summer of 1920, he accepted a post
as a Reader with the University of Leeds.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:56.250
At Leeds, he taught and collaborated with
other authors, continued writing The Book

00:10:56.250 --> 00:11:01.420
of Lost Tales, constructed languages, and
founded reading and social clubs like the

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:06.170
“Viking Club,” where undergraduates had
an affinity for Old Norse sagas and drinking

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:07.170
beer.

00:11:07.170 --> 00:11:12.740
In 1925, Tolkien finally received his professorship
at Oxford, the Rawlinson and Bosworth Professorship

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:14.149
of Anglo-Saxon.

00:11:14.149 --> 00:11:18.680
Tolkien was right at home in academia and
fit in remarkably well with the predominantly

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:19.759
male culture.

00:11:19.759 --> 00:11:24.410
He reveled in the lectures, research, and
exchange of ideas with students and fellow

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.410
professors.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:29.639
Tolkien did not publish many scholarly articles
yet he was extremely influential.

00:11:29.639 --> 00:11:34.170
One lecture worth mentioning altered the modern
study of the Old English epic tale Beowulf

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.769
and was first delivered in 1936.

00:11:36.769 --> 00:11:41.290
In “Beowulf, the Monsters and the Critics,”
Tolkien argued the monsters: Grendel, Grendel’s

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:46.290
mother, and the Dragon, are not merely extraneous
to the narrative but should be a focus of

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:47.290
study.

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:51.430
Tolkien believed critics put too much emphasis
on the historical elements of the tale instead

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:53.680
of looking at it as a work of art.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:56.180
At Oxford, Tolkien befriended colleague C.S.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:59.110
Lewis, best known for his fantasy series,
The Chronicles of Narnia.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:04.009
The two men bonded over their shared love
of mythology and began meeting regularly for

00:12:04.009 --> 00:12:07.410
a glass, a joke, and to criticize each other’s
poetry.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.779
The meetings were so enjoyable and useful,
they invited others to join.

00:12:10.779 --> 00:12:15.259
The informal group, known as “The Inklings”
eventually grew to 19 members and they met

00:12:15.259 --> 00:12:19.399
once a week, late at night, sometimes not
wrapping up until two or three o’clock in

00:12:19.399 --> 00:12:20.399
the morning.

00:12:20.399 --> 00:12:24.209
As was the practice, Tolkien shared manuscripts
of works-in-progress with The Inklings and

00:12:24.209 --> 00:12:26.709
received energetic feedback from the group.

00:12:26.709 --> 00:12:31.100
Among other writings, Tolkien brought original
poetry, sections from The Hobbit, excerpts

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:35.839
from “The Notion Club Papers,” and each
new chapter of The Lord of the Rings.

00:12:35.839 --> 00:12:39.720
There is little evidence to support the suggestion
by some that the men had a more spiritual

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:41.831
purpose to their meetings, or an “inkling”
of the Divine Nature.

00:12:41.831 --> 00:12:45.560
The Inklings continued to meet regularly for
19 years.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:49.449
Together with Tolkien and Lewis, some of the
more distinguished members of The Inklings

00:12:49.449 --> 00:12:54.149
included Neville Coghill, Hugo Dyson, Owen
Barfield, and Charles Williams.

00:12:54.149 --> 00:12:59.460
In 1945 Tolkien changed his chair at Oxford
to the Merton Professorship of English Language

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:05.120
and Literature, which he held until his retirement
in 1959.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:08.110
The Storyteller

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:12.839
One hot summer day in 1928, Professor Tolkien
was grading exam papers, which he described

00:13:12.839 --> 00:13:13.990
as “soul-destroying.”

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:18.529
He came upon a blank page — and without
thought —wrote down, “In a hole in the

00:13:18.529 --> 00:13:20.110
ground there lived a hobbit.”

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:21.279
But, What was a hobbit?

00:13:21.279 --> 00:13:23.300
And, Why did it live in the ground?

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:26.029
Tolkien needed to find the answers to these
questions.

00:13:26.029 --> 00:13:29.430
He said later, “Names always generate a
story in my mind.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:32.330
I thought I’d better find out what hobbits
were like.”

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:37.389
Then, in true Tolkien fashion, he dove headlong
into the creative process and concocted a

00:13:37.389 --> 00:13:41.380
tale to tell his younger children, and share
amongst The Inklings.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:46.250
In 1936, an incomplete copy of The Hobbit
wound up in Susan Dagnall’s hands, an employee

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:48.819
of the publishing firm of George Allen and
Unwin.

00:13:48.819 --> 00:13:53.420
Recognizing the story’s potential, Dagnall
convinced Tolkien to finish it and when complete,

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:55.220
she presented it to her boss.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:59.180
He then tested it out on his 10-year old son
who gave it a raving review.

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:03.839
The Hobbit was published one year later in
1937, and was an immediate hit.

00:14:03.839 --> 00:14:09.180
In fact, it was so successful, the publisher
asked Tolkien if he had any similar stories.

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:14.360
Today, since the first publication, The Hobbit
has sold over 100 million copies around the

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:19.380
world and has been translated in over 50 languages.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:20.939
What makes The Hobbit so enduring?

00:14:20.939 --> 00:14:24.899
For one thing, it lacks female characters
and it is not, nor ever has been, politically

00:14:24.899 --> 00:14:25.899
correct.

00:14:25.899 --> 00:14:30.450
It is also a very long tale with poetry, and
unlike other children’s fiction, does not

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:35.019
have a central child figure for whom young
readers can easily identify with.

00:14:35.019 --> 00:14:39.100
Although, the protagonist Bilbo Baggins is
“only a little hobbit,” so he kind of

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:40.829
acts like a surrogate child.

00:14:40.829 --> 00:14:45.040
Tolkien’s colorful descriptions of Middle-earth
and its complex characters (goblins, elves,

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:48.970
orcs, wizards, dragons, and hobbits of course)
are richly portrayed.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:54.149
And for all the fantasy writers who came after
Tolkien, hardly any can say their worlds were

00:14:54.149 --> 00:14:57.490
not, at least in part, influenced by The Hobbit.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:02.709
But, what set the story apart is the depth
of emotion and moral courage Tolkien weaves

00:15:02.709 --> 00:15:04.360
into his heroic fiction.

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:08.170
There are examples of this throughout The
Hobbit including the death of dwarf leader

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:13.230
Thorin Oakenshield, and Bilbo’s internal
struggles to do what is right — betraying

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:17.459
his friends while they try to reclaim the
Lonely Mountain from Smaug the dragon.

00:15:17.459 --> 00:15:22.680
Bilbo feels an obsessive greed has overtaken
Thorin and when Bilbo finds the Arkenstone,

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:27.180
the greatest treasure of all, he decides to
first hide it and then give it to his friends’

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:29.630
besiegers to be used as a bargaining chip.

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:34.949
In the end Bilbo exposes himself and confesses
because after all, they are friends.

00:15:34.949 --> 00:15:39.430
After Tolkien’s publication of The Hobbit,
he presented portions of The Silmarillion,

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:44.050
including incomplete stories of Lúthien and
Beren, to Stanley Unwin hoping for a warm

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:48.389
reception but his reader felt the stories
were not commercially publishable.

00:15:48.389 --> 00:15:50.360
They contained too much poetry.

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:54.610
Tolkien was disappointed at the news but soon
found himself busy writing the sequel to The

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:55.610
Hobbit.

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:59.410
Tolkien’s opus, what would become The Lord
of the Rings, was first published in three

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:02.870
parts: The Fellowship of the Ring, The Two
Towers, and The Return of the King between

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.730
1954 and 1955.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.680
And, it took him over a decade to write it.

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:11.870
Unwin’s son, who was by now an adult, was
heavily involved in pushing a tempermental

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.720
Tolkien along to finish it.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:18.309
Thinking it would be a relative unimpressive
release, and a loss to the firm, the publishers

00:16:18.309 --> 00:16:21.510
grossly underestimated The Lord of the Rings
public appeal.

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:25.550
True, it had mixed reviews — from damning
to glowing and everything in between.

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:30.050
BBC adapted it into 12 condensed episodes,
elevating its popularity further.

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:34.540
Then, in the mid-1960s a pirated paperback
version was released which caught the attention

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:35.699
of American readers.

00:16:35.699 --> 00:16:41.129
A sort of cult developed based on the newfound
popularity of fantasy literature and Tolkien

00:16:41.129 --> 00:16:42.629
was made a rich man.

00:16:42.629 --> 00:16:45.259
He was not entirely happy though, even if
he was flattered.

00:16:45.259 --> 00:16:50.889
Partly, because rumors circulated of party-going
cult readers ingesting LSD and reading The

00:16:50.889 --> 00:16:52.019
Lords of the Rings.

00:16:52.019 --> 00:16:56.980
And some overzealous fans, who Tolkien referred
to as lunatics, were calling his home demanding

00:16:56.980 --> 00:17:00.029
to know if Frodo had succeeded in his quest.

00:17:00.029 --> 00:17:03.939
The Hobbit and The Lord of the Rings certainly
receive all the glory but Tolkien authored

00:17:03.939 --> 00:17:08.390
a number of other articles and essays during
his lifetime including: The Monsters and the

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:12.180
Critics and Other Essays; one Middle-earth
related work, The Adventures of Tom Bombadil;

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:17.090
editions and translations of Middle English
works such as the Ancrene Wisse, Sir Gawain,

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:22.910
Sir Orfeo and The Pearl, and stories the Imram,
The Homecoming of Beorhtnoth Beorhthelm’s

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:28.780
Son, The Lay of Aotrou and Itroun, Farmer
Giles of Ham, Leaf by Niggle, and Smith of

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:29.780
Wootton Major.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:34.440
Following his death, The Letters from Father
Christmas were released by the Tolkien estate,

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:38.610
and later, son Christopher saw to it that
his father’s Silmarillion and a number of

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:43.530
other incomplete writings under the title
of Unfinished Tales of Númenor and Middle-earth

00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:44.530
were published.

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:50.070
After his retirement from Oxford Tolkien moved
to Bournemouth and on November 29, 1971 the

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:51.750
love of his life, Edith died.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:56.090
Nearly two years later on September 2, 1973
Tolkien followed.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:18:00.420
As a final testament to their love, and at
Tolkien’s instruction, they were buried

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:01.770
in a single grave.

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:07.950
On their tombstone, "Beren" is engraved under
his name and "Luthien" appears under Edith’s.

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:11.200
Accomplishments &amp; Legacy

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:15.320
Tolkien shall remain a celebrated literary
figure through the ages as his life work continues

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.430
to inspire the fantasy genre.

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:21.620
Around the world, his characters and places
have become the namesake of various street

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.640
names, companies, mountains, plants, and objects.

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:29.260
There are even asteroids named after Bilbo
Baggins and Tolkien himself.

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:34.050
In England, there are seven blue plaques that
commemorate places associated with Tolkien.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:37.570
Tolkien was made a Commander of the Order
of the British Empire by Queen Elizabeth II

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:38.570
in 1972.

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:42.670
And, he holds a number of other achievements
and awards including: an honorary degree from

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:47.370
The National University of Ireland and University
of Liege in 1954, and the Locus Award for

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:50.200
Best Fantasy novel for The Silmarillion in
1978.

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:54.550
In the 2000s, Tolkien ranked on BBC’s ‘greatest
Britons’ list and The Lord of the Rings

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:59.460
was the UK’s ‘best loved novel’ (2003)
and ranked among ‘The 100 Greatest British

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:00.820
Novels’ (2015).

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:05.900
Tolkien was placed sixth on the list of ‘The
50 greatest British writers since 1945’

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:08.270
published by ‘The Times’ in 2008.

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:12.580
In 2009, he was listed as the fifth top-earning
‘dead celebrity’ by Forbes.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:17.680
From 2001 to 2003, New Line Cinema released
The Lord of the Rings as a trilogy directed

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:18.680
by Peter Jackson.

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:22.790
The series was extremely successful and won
numerous Oscars.

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:28.300
From 2012 to 2014, Warner Bros. and New Line
Cinema released The Hobbit, a series of three

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:29.950
films based on The Hobbit.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:35.780
The first in 2012, The Hobbit: An Unexpected
Journey, the second in 2013, The Hobbit: The

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:41.030
Desolation of Smaug, and the final instalment
in 2014, The Hobbit: The Battle of the Five

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:42.030
Armies.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:55.760
Most recently, Amazon retained the rights
to adapt The Lord of the Rings for its Prime

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:57.130
streaming service.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:03.340
The multi-season adaptation, will focus on
“previously unexplored stories based on

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.340
J.R.R.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:07.110
Tolkien’s original writings,” according
to a representative for the Tolkien Estate.

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:12.050
Tolkien’s Middle-earth is surely the gift
that keeps on giving.

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:22.730
And It is quite amazing, considering he wrote
it all in his spare time.

